# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore template -- keeps the build context small and keeps secrets
# and local-only files out of the image entirely. Pairs with the Dockerfile
# in this same resource and with Chapter 6, Lesson 26 (Environment
# Configuration & Secrets) -- .env must never reach an image layer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies -- reinstalled fresh inside the image by `npm ci`; copying the
# host's node_modules in would both bloat the build context and risk
# shipping host-specific native binaries that don't match the base image.
node_modules
npm-debug.log

# Version control -- irrelevant to the running container and often large.
.git
.gitignore

# Environment & secrets -- never let these cross into an image layer, even
# though .dockerignore is a different mechanism from .gitignore.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

# Build output and caches that get regenerated inside the image anyway.
dist
build
coverage
.cache

# Editor/OS cruft.
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Project-local tooling that has no business inside the image.
docker-compose.yml
compose.yaml
Dockerfile*
README.md
NOTES.md

# Tests -- the runtime image doesn't need them; CI runs tests against the
# build stage or a separate test target before the image is ever pushed.
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js
__tests__/
